{"id": "b327774f-1452-4c7e-985a-dc7c713754fe", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:30:12.515600", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "c048df4c-12e4-49d3-9ae7-f2626bf9dfce", "action": {"command": "cat > /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n# Experiment Design — Do OPRO-optimized instructions outperform baselines on BBH?\n\n> Document type: **Design-only** (paper-faithful reconstruction). No experiments executed. No measured outcomes. All numeric blocks in this document are *specifications of computations or targets*, never reported results.\n> Runtime target of this design: **bubblewrap / no-network / no-GPU** (analytics via Python stdlib + locally produced CSVs only). External LLM inference is *deferred to an execution environment outside the bubblewrap* (see §g).\n> All decisions in §b–§l are **pre-registered** as fixed-then-fact; deviations require explicit justification in §h.\n\n---\n\n## (a) Goal & research question\n\n**Research question.** *Do the optimized instructions discovered by OPRO outperform the baseline instructions (\"Let's think step by step.\" and the empty prompt) on BBH tasks?*\n\n**Operationalization.** \"Outperform\" is operationalized as a strictly larger task-averaged accuracy on the **full BBH canary/eval split (≈6,511 examples across 27 tasks, ≤250 / task)**, holding the LLM, the prompt *format* and the decoding policy constant. The comparison is **per-task paired** so that the instruction-string factor is the sole varying input — this rules out confounds due to task-mix.\n\n**Primary deliverable.** A point estimate and 95 % Wilson CI for `Δ_macro = macro_acc(OPRO-best) − macro_acc(baseline)`, separately for each baseline, with a per-task McNemar test + FDR-BH and a paired Wilcoxon aggregate.\n\n**Out of scope.** (i) Whether OPRO *itself* improves across iterations (that's an OPRO-internal ablation); (ii) any inject of non-OPRO instruction sources (AutoPrompt, \"Chain-of-Thought\" prompts from other works, etc.); (iii) anything that changes prompt *format* between instruction conditions.\n\nDESIGN_EOF\necho \"wrote_part_1\"; wc -l /workspace/experiment_design.md", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-ee138052-691f-420e-8aaa-89b00cb813f4", "tool_call": {"id": "call-ee138052-691f-420e-8aaa-89b00cb813f4", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Stage 1 of doc\", \"command\": \"cat > /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\\n# Experiment Design \\u2014 Do OPRO-optimized instructions outperform baselines on BBH?\\n\\n> Document type: **Design-only** (paper-faithful reconstruction). No experiments executed. No measured outcomes. All numeric blocks in this document are *specifications of computations or targets*, never reported results.\\n> Runtime target of this design: **bubblewrap / no-network / no-GPU** (analytics via Python stdlib + locally produced CSVs only). External LLM inference is *deferred to an execution environment outside the bubblewrap* (see \\u00a7g).\\n> All decisions in \\u00a7b\\u2013\\u00a7l are **pre-registered** as fixed-then-fact; deviations require explicit justification in \\u00a7h.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (a) Goal & research question\\n\\n**Research question.** *Do the optimized instructions discovered by OPRO outperform the baseline instructions (\\\"Let's think step by step.\\\" and the empty prompt) on BBH tasks?*\\n\\n**Operationalization.** \\\"Outperform\\\" is operationalized as a strictly larger task-averaged accuracy on the **full BBH canary/eval split (\\u22486,511 examples across 27 tasks, \\u2264250 / task)**, holding the LLM, the prompt *format* and the decoding policy constant. The comparison is **per-task paired** so that the instruction-string factor is the sole varying input \\u2014 this rules out confounds due to task-mix.\\n\\n**Primary deliverable.** A point estimate and 95 % Wilson CI for `\\u0394_macro = macro_acc(OPRO-best) \\u2212 macro_acc(baseline)`, separately for each baseline, with a per-task McNemar test + FDR-BH and a paired Wilcoxon aggregate.\\n\\n**Out of scope.** (i) Whether OPRO *itself* improves across iterations (that's an OPRO-internal ablation); (ii) any inject of non-OPRO instruction sources (AutoPrompt, \\\"Chain-of-Thought\\\" prompts from other works, etc.); (iii) anything that changes prompt *format* between instruction conditions.\\n\\nDESIGN_EOF\\necho \\\"wrote_part_1\\\"; wc -l /workspace/experiment_design.md\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-55518614-b6a5-44df-81b6-5fca7d695170", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 23}
