 and a paired Wilcoxon aggregate.\\n\\n**Out of scope.** (i) Whether OPRO *itself* improves across iterations (that's an OPRO-internal ablation); (ii) any inject of non-OPRO instruction sources (AutoPrompt, \\\"Chain-of-Thought\\\" prompts from other works, etc.); (iii) anything that changes prompt *format* between instruction conditions.\\n\\nDESIGN_EOF\\necho \\\"wrote_part_1\\\"; wc -l /workspace/experiment_design.md\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.016, \"output\": \"wrote_part_1\\n18 /workspace/experiment_design.md\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "b327774f-1452-4c7e-985a-dc7c713754fe", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 24}
{"id": "26a6ee8f-0a54-415a-babb-bc86a78c3262", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:30:22.501692", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "1fb36296-897d-4f33-b41a-9fe951b6d245", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n---\n\n## (b) Hypotheses & pre-registration table\n\n**Hypothesis ordering (locked; primary → secondary):**\n\n| Rank | ID | Comparison | Type | α (per-comparison) | MCP | N (analytic units) |\n|------|----|------------|------|--------------------|-----|--------------------|\n| **Primary** | **H1\\_1** | `OPRO-best > empty prompt` | one-sided, superiority | 0.025 (one-sided) | FDR-BH q=0.05 across 27 tasks | 27 task-level paired accuracies + 27×2 example-level binarized disagreement tables for McNemar |\n| Secondary | H1\\_2 | `OPRO-best > \"Let's think step by step.\"` | one-sided, superiority | 0.025 (one-sided) | FDR-BH q=0.05 across 27 tasks | as above |\n| Tertiary (only if published) | H2\\_k | `OPRO top-k (k∈{3,5})` family vs LTSBS / empty | one-sided, descriptive | 0.025 (one-sided) | FDR-BH q=0.05 | as above |\n\nFormal pre-registrations (H0/H1 per self-contained entry):\n\n* **H1\\_1_null**: `task_acc(OPRO-best) ≤ task_acc(empty)` at every task i ∈ {1..27}; **H1\\_1_alt**: strict superiority in `macro_acc` AND echo in `micro_acc` with FDR-controlled per-task McNemar.\n* **H1\\_2_null**: `task_acc(OPRO-best) ≤ task_acc(LTSBS)`; **H1\\_2_alt**: same dual criterion.\n* **Aggregate test**: one-sided paired **Wilcoxon signed-rank** on the 27 pairs of `task_acc` (OPRO vs baseline), with **Holm** correction across k=2 baselines (k_{Holm}=2 family).\n* **Effect size (aggregate)**: `rank-biserial r` from Wilcoxon + **bootstrap 95 % CI** of `Δ_macro` from B=10 000 task-level resamples (with replacement).\n\n**Decision rule (locked):** primary claim \"OPRO outperforms baseline X\" succeeds iff *both* (i) per-task McNemar shows at most 1 loss at q<0.05 *and* (ii) aggregate Wilcoxon p<α_{Holm,2} *and* (iii) bootstrap CI for `Δ_macro