{"id": "06e14326-e060-401a-ab7d-029c9a994414", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:31:27.024681", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "68255c07-99d3-4857-ba93-d8e44616cfc0", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n---\n\n## (e) Statistical plan — locked formulas and decision rule\n\n### e.1 Notation (worked)\n\n* `I ∈ {OPRO_best, LTSBS, empty}` — instruction\n* `t ∈ T = {1..27}` — task index\n* `n_t` — number of examples in BBH task t\n* `x_{t,i}^I ∈ {0,1}` — binary correctness of instruction `I` on task `t` example `i`\n* `acc_t^I = (1/n_t) Σ_i x_{t,i}^I` — per-task accuracy\n* `macro^I = (1/27) Σ_t acc_t^I` — macro-accuracy across tasks\n* `micro^I = (Σ_t n_t · acc_t^I) / (Σ_t n_t)` — micro-accuracy\n\n### e.2 Per-task paired test\n\nFor each (task t, baseline B), build the 2×2 disagreement table on the common example index:\n\n* `b_01^B(t) = Σ_i [x_{t,i}^{OPRO-best}=0 ∧ x_{t,i}^{B}=1]` — examples where baseline wins\n* `b_10^B(t) = Σ_i [x_{t,i}^{OPRO-best}=1 ∧ x_{t,i}^{B}=0]` — examples where OPRO-best wins\n\nApply **exact one-sided McNemar's test** with continuity-corrected chi-squared fallback if `b_01+b_10 ≥ 25`; use exact binomial otherwise. Compute statistic:\n\n```\nχ^2_Mc(t,B) = (|b_10 - b_01| - 1)^2 / (b_10 + b_01)\n```\n\n*Per-task effect size:* `OR^B(t) = inf safe`; report `odds ratio = b_10 / b_01` (with 0.5 Haldane–Anscombe correction if any cell is 0) and `Cohen's d_t^B` on `acc_t^{OPRO-best} − acc_t^B` (interpreted per-task as raw difference, since SE of difference depends on intra-example correlation).\n\n### e.3 MCP across 27 per-task tests\n\nApply **Benjamini–Hochberg FDR** at q=0.05 over the combined 27×k_B tests where k_B = 2 baselines (or 3 if top-k arm is included). Adjusted `p_FDR(t,B)` is what the decision rule reads.\n\n### e.4 Aggregate test\n\nFor each baseline B:\n\n* Compute `Δ_t^B = acc_t^{OPRO-best} − acc_t^B` for t ∈ 1..27\n* Apply one-sided **paired Wilcoxon signed-rank** with `pratt` zero-handling; report `r_rb = 1 − 2W/(n(n+1)/2)` (rank-biserial) and one-sided p-value\n* Apply **Holm** step-down across the k=2 → 2 ordered p-values (one per baseline), enforce `α_{Holm,2} = {0.025, 0.05}` per comparison-wise α=0.025\n\n### e.5 Bootstrap CI for Δ_macro\n\n`B = 10 000` resamples of the 27 tasks with replacement (numpy / stdlib `random.choices`); compute `Δ_macro^{(b)}`; report 2.5% / 97.5% percentiles (BCa if `sklearn` unavailable → non-BCa percentile-only CI is acceptable; flagged in §h).\n\n### e.6 Wilson CI per condition\n\nFor each I: `acc^I_macro`, `acc^I_micro`: 95 % Wilson CI; for per-task acc, Wilson on `Σ_i x_{t,i}^I / n_t` (Wilson-only, no continuity corrections reported unless sample size < 30).\n\n### e.7 Hypothesis matrix (locked)\n\n| Hypothesis | Claim | α (one-sided) | MCP family | Stats tests in family | Decision rule shortcut |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| H1_1 (primary) | `Δ^empty_macro > 0` AND Δ^empty_{t,i} paired ≡ superiority | 0.025 | FDR-BH(q=0.05) over 27 + Holm-adjusted aggregate | McNemar × 27 + Wilcoxon (+ Holm) | all four sub-criteria must hold |\n| H1_2 (secondary) | same vs LTSBS | 0.025 | same | same | same |\n| H2_k (tertiary, optional) | OPRO-top-k vs each baseline | 0.025 | FDR-BH + Holm per k | same | descriptive; not part of primary claim |\n\n### e.8 Failure-handling matrix (pre-registered)\n\n| Pattern observed | Verdict | Reporting |\n|---|---|---|\n| McNemar zero significant per-task AND Wilcoxon sig AND bootstrap CI excludes 0 AND micro and macro agree | primary claim **made** | Table 1, Figure forest-plot |\n| McNemar noisy but aggregate sig AND bootstrap CI excludes 0 | \"partial effect — declared as macro-level only\" | Table 1 with both views |\n| Aggregate Wilcoxon sig but bootstrap CI for Δ_macro straddles 0 | \"inconclusive\" — neither claim made | report both |\n| Sign flip across macro vs micro | \"magnitude-not-typicality effect\" — no primary claim | report both with raw counts |\n| One task dominates the per-task effect | secondary AUC-style Welch sensitivity over `n_t` weights reported | separate row |\n\nDESIGN_EOF\necho \"wrote_part_5\"; wc -l /workspace/experiment_design.md", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-172a5843-82bd-478d-bdbc-b35f20ec9790", "tool_call": {"id": "call-172a5843-82bd-478d-bdbc-b35f20ec9790", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Stage 5 \\u2014 statistical plan\", \"command\": \"cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\\n---\\n\\n## (e) Statistical plan \\u2014 locked formulas and decision rule\\n\\n### e.1 Notation (worked)\\n\\n* `I \\u2208 {OPRO_best, LTSBS, empty}` \\u2014 instruction\\n* `t \\u2208 T = {1..27}` \\u2014 task index\\n* `n_t` \\u2014 number of examples in BBH task t\\n* `x_{t,i}^I \\u2208 {0,1}` \\u2014 binary correctness of instruction `I` on task `t` example `i`\\n* `acc_t^I = (1/n_t) \\u03a3_i x_{t,i}^I` \\u2014 per-task accuracy\\n* `macro^I = (1/27) \\u03a3_t acc_t^I` \\u2014 macro-accuracy across tasks\\n* `micro^I = (\\u03a3_t n_t \\u00b7 acc_t^I) / (\\u03a3_t n_t)` \\u2014 micro-accuracy\\n\\n### e.2 Per-task paired test\\n\\nFor each (task t, baseline B), build the 2\\u00d72 disagreement table on the common example index:\\n\\n* `b_01^B(t) = \\u03a3_i [x_{t,i}^{OPRO-best}=0 \\u2227 x_{t,i}^{B}=1]` \\u2014 examples where baseline wins\\n* `b_10^B(t) = \\u03a3_i [x_{t,i}^{OPRO-best}=1 \\u2227 x_{t,i}^{B}=0]` \\u2014 examples where OPRO-best wins\\n\\nApply **exact one-sided McNemar's test** with continuity-corrected chi-squared fallback if `b_01+b_10 \\u2265 25`; use exact binomial otherwise. Compute statistic:\\n\\n```\\n\\u03c7^2_Mc(t,B) = (|b_10 - b_01| - 1)^2 / (b_10 + b_01)\\n```\\n\\n*Per-task effect size:* `OR^B(t) = inf safe`; report `odds ratio = b_10 / b_01` (with 0.5 Haldane\\u2013Anscombe correction if any cell is 0) and `Cohen's d_t^B` on `acc_t^{OPRO-best} \\u2212 acc_t^B` (interpr