{"id": "c99068a3-503a-4399-a85e-948615369a39", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:31:58.228192", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "ec282a65-8bc3-466b-adbf-ad78a9e5b222", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n---\n\n## (f) Implementation spec — pseudocode (deferred-to-executable skeleton)\n\n### f.1 — Paired inference loop (paper-faithful, designed for external env in production)\n\n```python\n# Pseudocode only — not meant to run in bubblewrap as-is; it's a contract.\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Iterable, Dict, Tuple\nimport csv, json, os, random, time, hashlib\n\n# ----- (1) config -----\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Config:\n    llm_alias: str\n    instructions: Tuple[str, ...]      # ('OPRO_best', 'LTSBS', 'empty')\n    fewshot_mode: str                  # '0-shot' or '3-shot'\n    template: str                      # \"Q: {input}\\nA:\"\n    temperature: float                 # 0.0 primary\n    top_p: float                       # 1.0\n    max_output_tokens: int             # 512\n    out_dir: str\n    seed_optional: int                 # only for sensitivity arm\n\n# ----- (2) audit -----\ndef audit_instructions(instructions_path: str, instr_id: str, text: str) -> str:\n    p = os.path.join(instructions_path, instr_id + \".txt\")\n    with open(p, \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(text.strip())\n    return hashlib.sha256(open(p, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest() + \"  \" + p\n\n# ----- (3) prompt assembly -----\ndef build_prompt(instruction_text: str, item: dict, fewshot_block: str = \"\") -> str:\n    instr = instruction_text.strip()\n    if instr == \"\":\n        return f\"{fewshot_block}Q: {item['input']}\\nA:\"\n    return f\"{instr}\\n{fewshot_block}Q: {item['input']}\\nA:\"\n\n# ----- (4) inference (one cell = (instruction, task)) -----\ndef run_cell(cfg: Config, llm_client, instruction_text: str, task_data: Iterable[dict],\n             fewshot_block: str = \"\", out_csv: str = \"\") -> Dict:\n    rows, paired_pred = [], []\n    for item in task_data:\n        prompt = build_prompt(instruction_text, item, fewshot_block)\n        resp = llm_client.complete(\n            prompt=prompt,\n            temperature=cfg.temperature, top_p=cfg.top_p,\n            max_output_tokens=cfg.max_output_tokens)\n        pred = bbhh_extract_final_answer(resp.text, task_id=item[\"task_id\"])\n        rows.append({\"id\": item[\"id\"], \"raw\": resp.text, \"pred\": pred,\n                     \"gold\": item[\"gold\"], \"correct\": int(pred == item[\"gold\"])})\n    # output paired CSV keyed by example-id (paired across (instruction) cells)\n    if out_csv:\n        with open(out_csv, \"w\") as f:\n            w = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=rows[0].keys())\n            w.writeheader(); w.writerows(rows)\n    return {\"n\": len(rows), \"acc\": sum(r[\"correct\"] for r in rows) / len(rows)}\n\n# ----- (5) pairing across instructions -----\ndef pair_across_instructions(out_dir: str, task_id: str, instr_ids=(\"OPRO_best\",\"LTSBS\",\"empty\")):\n    \"\"\"Load per-instruction CSVs and join on example-id; produce 27 paired tables.\n       These tables are the canonical input to McNemar (§e.2) and to Δ_t (§e.4).\"\"\"\n    tables = {I: read_csv(os.path.join(out_dir, f\"{task_id}__{I}.csv\")) for I in instr_ids}\n    base = tables[\"OPRO_best\"][[\"id\",\"correct\"]].rename(columns={\"correct\":\"OPRO_best\"})\n    for I in (\"LTSBS\",\"empty\"):\n        base = base.merge(tables[I][[\"id\",\"correct\"]].rename(columns={\"correct\":I}), on=\"id\")\n    return base  # one row per example, three correctness columns\n\n# ----- (6) top-level driver -----\ndef main(cfg: Config):\n    os.makedirs(cfg.out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    # 3a. audit\n    for I, t in zip((\"OPRO_best\",\"LTSBS\",\"empty\"),\n                    (\"Take a deep breath and work on this problem step-by-step.\",\n                     \"Let's think step by step.\", \"\")):\n        print(I, audit_instructions(cfg.out_dir, I, t))\n    # 3b. iterate\n    for task_id, examples in load_bbh_split(out_dir + \"/bbh\"):       # length 27\n        for I, t in zip((\"OPRO_best\",\"LTSBS\",\"empty\"),\n                        (\"Take a deep breath and work on this problem step-by-step.\",\n                         \"Let's think step by step.\", \"\")):\n            run_cell(cfg, llm_client=make_client(cfg.llm_alias),\n                     instruction_text=t, task_data=examples,\n                     out_csv=os.path.join(cfg.out_dir, f\"{task_id}__{I}.csv\"))\n        # 3c. emit paired table for this task\n        pair_across_instructions(cfg.out_dir, task_id).to_csv(\n            os.path.join(cfg.out_dir, f\"{task_id}__paired.csv\"), index=False)\n```\n\n### f.2 — BBH-style answer extraction (paper-faithful regex contract)\n\nPseudocode of the BBH evaluation extraction logic (read-only description; actual implementation outside bubblewrap):\n\n```\nfunction bbhh_extract_final_answer(raw_output, task_id):\n    # 1) Hard preference for \"Final Answer:\" marker (BBH convention).\n    m = regex.search(r'(?is)final\\s*answer\\s*[:：\\-]\\s*([^\\n]+)', raw_output)\n    if m: return normalize(m.group(1))\n\n    # 2) Pattern: \"the answer is X\" / \"answer: X\"\n    m = regex.search(r'(?is)\\bthe\\s+answer\\s+is\\s+[:：\\-]?\\s*([^\\n\\.]+)', raw_output)\n    if m: return normalize(m.group(1))\n    m = regex.search(r'(?is)\\banswer\\s*[:：\\-]\\s*([^\\n\\.]+)', raw_output)\n    if m: return normalize(m.group(1))\n\n    # 3) For multiple-choice tasks: take the first A–Z (or (A)–(Z)) token in the\n    #    FINAL line of the output (i.e. the line after the last newline-emptied segment).\n    if task_id in MC_TASK_IDS:\n        for line in reversed(raw_output.splitlines()[::-1]):\n            line = line.strip()\n            if line == \"\": continue\n            m = regex.search(r'^\\(?([A-Z])\\)?[\\.\\):]?\\s', line)\n            if m: return m.group(1)\n            # take the first uppercase Latin letter on the line\n            first_letter = regex.search(r'\\b([A-Z])\\b', line)\n            if first_letter: return first_letter.group(1)\n            break       # we only look at the final non-empty line\n\n    # 4) Otherwise normalize and return the final non-empty line.\n    final_lines = [l.strip() for l in raw_output.splitlines() if l.strip()]\n    return normalize(final_lines[-1] if final_lines else \"\")\n```\n\n`normalize(x)` does: lowercase, strip surrounding whitespace, strip an outer pair of parens, strip a leading/trailing period/comma, collapse internal whitespace.\n\n> The above is a *specification*. The actual external implementation must be byte-equivalent to the BBH official scorer or re-derive it by side-test against the released one on a held-in 50-example golden set (recorded in §h limits).\n\n### f.3 — Statistical computation (PsStdlib-safe skeleton)\n\nThis skeleton is **designed to run inside bubblewrap** (Python `csv`+`math`+`random`+`statistics` only; no `numpy`/`scipy`):\n\n```python\nimport csv, math, random, statistics, hashlib, os, json\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nINSTRUCTIONS = [\"OPRO_best\",\"LTSBS\",\"empty\"]\nPAIRED_DIR    = \"/workspace/runs/paired\"          # input: 27 paired CSVs\n\ndef wilson_ci(p, n, z=1.96):\n    if n==0: return (0.,1.)\n    denom = 1 + z*z/n\n    centre = (p + z*z/(2*n))/denom\n    half = (z*math.sqrt(p*(1-p)/n + z*z/(4*n*n)))/denom\n    return (max(0.,centre-half), min(1.,centre+half))\n\ndef mcnemar(b10, b01):\n    # continuity-corrected chi-square; for b10+b01 < 25 use exact later\n    if b10+b01 == 0: return 1.0\n    return ((abs(b10-b01)-1)**2) / (b10+b01)   # chi-square with df=1\n\ndef bh_fdr(pvals, q=0.05):\n    n = len(pvals); idx = sorted(range(n), key=lambda i: pvals[i])\n    adj = [0.0]*n\n    prev = 1.0\n    for rank,i in enumerate(reversed(idx), start=1):\n        k = n - rank + 1\n        v = min(prev, pvals[i]*n/k)\n        adj[i] = v; prev = v\n    return adj\n\ndef paired_wilcoxon(delt