{"id": "cc5e28b1-a098-493e-998f-11527325474f", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T02:32:16.342296", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "9b250857-1a2a-470f-8dfc-be395dbc943a", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n---\n\n## (g) Feasibility & runtime plan\n\n### g.1 — Call budget (computational)\n\n| LLM | Cells per task | Examples per task | Subtotal cells | Subtotal calls |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| primary (text-bison / PaLM 2-L) | 3 (OPRO-best, LTSBS, empty) | ≤250 | 27 × 3 = 81 | 27 × 3 × ≤250 ≈ ≤ **20,250** |\n| secondary (`gpt-3.5-turbo-0613`) [optional] | 3 | ≤250 | 81 | ≤ **20,250** |\n| secondary (`gpt-4-0613`) [optional] | 3 | ≤250 | 81 | ≤ **20,250** |\n| 3-shot ablation (primary LLM only) [optional] | 3 | ≤250 | 81 | ≤ **20,250** |\n| sensitivity arm (n_seeds=3, T=0.7, primary LLM only) [optional] | 3 × 3 | ≤250 | 27 × 9 = 243 | ≤ **60,750** |\n| trimming sensitivity (`OPRO-best-trimmed-to-LTSBS-length`) [post-hoc, optional] | 1 | ≤250 | 27 | ≤ 6,750 |\n\nPrimary-only baseline: **≈ 20,250 LLM calls** (no Fab claim — it's a specification of how many calls *would* be issued).\n\n### g.2 — Token budget (specification only — verified at run-time)\n\n| LLM | Input tokens / call (spec) | Output tokens / call (spec) | Total tokens / call | Total tokens (primary only) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| text-bison / PaLM 2-L | 200–1,500 (instruction + BBH input) | ≤ 512 | ~700–2,000 | ~ 14–40 M tokens total |\n| gpt-3.5-turbo-0613 | as above | ≤ 512 | ~700–2,000 | ~ 14–40 M tokens total |\n| gpt-4-0613 | as above | ≤ 512 | ~700–2,000 | ~ 14–40 M tokens total |\n\nThese ranges are derived from BBH input lengths ≲ 1,200 characters (≈ 400 tokens) × ~1.3× instruction overhead, plus max_output=512. Real measurement replaces these ranges in the final run.\n\n### g.3 — Latency / cost ranges (illustrative; replaced by measured at execution)\n\n> All numbers are **estimates** that must be replaced by the actual model's published pricing before any budget consumption. They are NOT measured run-experiments and are not used to claim any result.\n\n* `text-bison / PaLM 2-L` (Google pricing, ~$0.0005/1k chars in, ~$0.0015/1k chars out, illustrative) ⇒ primary-only rough order of magnitude ≤ ~$30 — **open-source verification**: replace with current Google AI Studio / Vertex AI rate card.\n* `gpt-3.5-turbo-0613` (~$0.0015/1k tok in, ~$0.002/1k tok out) ⇒ rough order ≤ ~$120.\n* `gpt-4-0613` (~$0.03/1k tok in, ~$0.06/1k tok out) ⇒ rough order ≤ ~$4,000 (do not run in sensitivity arm without explicit budget confirmation).\n\n> These figures only exist to express the *shape* of cost scaling: primary is the cheapest reliable path; sensitivity arm + cross-family + 3-shot together dwarf primary cost; GPT-4 is the cost-yield heavy option.\n\n### g.4 — Runtime environment mapping\n\n```yaml\nruntime_modes:\n  mode_a_internal_bubblewrap:\n    executes: \"audit, SHA-256 manifest, dry-run pairing integrity checks, statistical computation on simulated paired CSVs\"\n    does_NOT_execute: \"any real LLM call\"\n    libs_used: \"Python stdlib only (hashlib, csv, json, math, random, statistics, re, dataclasses)\"\n  mode_b_external_unprivileged:\n    executes: \"LLM calls, paired CSVs persistence, deferred statistical computation\"\n    required_secrets: \"google-genai or Vertex-AI token for text-bison; OPENAI_API_KEY for cross-family\"\n    libs_used: \"as needed (numpy, scipy, scikit-learn optional)\"\n    shutdown_procedure: \"all per-task CSVs, audit manifest, OPRO instruction bytes committed; raw `raw_output` columns discarded if budget prohibitions apply (rare; wekeep raw output for any future audit)\"\n```\n\n### g.5 — Stepwise execution checklist (paper-faithful path for mode A => mode B handoff)\n\n1. Place literal instructions in `/workspace/audit_files/`; generate `opr_best.txt`, `ltsbs.txt`, `empty.txt`.\n2. Compute SHA-256 hex digests and write into `/workspace/audit_files/audit_manifest.txt`.\n3. (mode B) For each LLM, issue calls per `f.1`; persist `{task}__OPRO_best.csv`, `{task}__LTSBS.csv`, `{task}__empty.csv`, then derive `{task}__paired.csv`.\n4. (mode A or B) Run `bootstrap_macro_diff_pairs` → collect point + 95 % CI for `Δ_macro_LTSBS`, `Δ_macro_empty`.\n5. Compute per-task McNemar p-values; apply BH-FDR; collect per-task `Δ_t`, `OR_t`, `Cohen's d_t`.\n6. Run aggregate paired Wilcoxon; apply Holm(k=2); record `r_rb` and adjusted p.\n7. Emit Table 1 (per-task MCN+OR+d, FDR-adjusted), Table 2 (aggregate: macro, micro, Wilson CI, Wilcoxon, Holm, bootstrap CI), Figure (forest-plot).\n8. File the mode-A audit bundle as `/workspace/audit_bundle.json` with all hashes, instruction bytes, config snapshot.\n\nDESIGN_EOF\necho \"wrote_part_7\"; wc -l /workspace/experiment_design.md", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-cd49ace2-7e1e-44bc-aab0-5b462aac5f22", "tool_call": {"id": "call-cd49ace2-7e1e-44bc-aab0-5b462aac5f22", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Stage 7 \\u2014 feasibility\", \"command\": \"cat >> /workspace/experiment_design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\\n---\\n\\n## (g) Feasibility & runtime plan\\n\\n### g.1 \\u2014 Call budget (computational)\\n\\n| LLM | Cells per task | Examples per task | Subtotal cells | Subtotal calls |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| primary (text-bison / PaLM 2-L) | 3 (OPRO-best, LTSBS, empty) | \\u2264250 | 27 \\u00d7 3 = 81 | 27 \\u00d7 3 \\u00d7 \\u2264250 \\u2248 \\u2264 **20,250** |\\n| secondary (`gpt-3.5-turbo-0613`) [optional] | 3 | \\u2264250 | 81 | \\u2264 **20,250** |\\n| secondary (`gpt-4-0613`) [optional] | 3 | \\u2264250 | 81 | \\u2264 **20,250** |\\n| 3-shot ablation (primary LLM only) [optional] | 3 | \\u2264250 | 81 | \\u2264 **20,250** |\\n| sensitivity arm (n_seeds=3, T=0.7, primary LLM only) [optional] | 3 \\u00d7 3 | \\u2264250 | 27 \\u00d7 9 = 243 | \\u2264 **60,750** |\\n| trimming sensitivity (`OPRO-best-trimmed-to-LTSBS-l